inalize the JSON content.\n- `chapter_id`: CH03\n- `title`: 机制通路：免疫、代谢与屏障功能的介导作用\n- `purpose`: 解析微生物群调节 ICI 疗效的分子与细胞机制，明确临床前因果证据与人类观察性数据的界限。\n- `scope`: 实体瘤；免疫细胞互作、代谢物信号、屏障功能；标注物种差异与肿瘤类型特异性。\n- `substantive_threads`: 4 threads as planned.\n- `supplement_requests`: 1 request on Human Strain-Specific Mechanism.\n- `directed_reads`: P0582, P0092, P0388, P0166, P0317.\n- `excluded_source_handles`: I will exclude sources that are purely about non-solid tumors without transferable mechanism (e.g., P0056 Hematologic, P0311 CAR-T specific if not transferable). But routing assigned them. I will keep them as \"available\" but note in the plan to use them only for general mechanism principles. I won't exclude them formally unless they are completely irrelevant. I'll leave `excluded_source_handles` empty or minimal to respect the routing, but I will note in `substantive_threads` how to handle them. Actually, the instruction says \"when an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\". P0056 (Hematologic) is routed to CH03/CH05. I can keep it for general mechanism (SCFA) but exclude it if I decide it's too specific to hematologic. I'll keep it as available for general SCFA mechanism but note the limitation. I will exclude P0311 (CAR-T) from *this* chapter if it doesn't discuss ICI mechanisms, but the routing says CH03. I'll keep it for parallel mechanism comparison. I will not exclude any routed sources to avoid conflict with routing, but I will prioritize solid tumor ones.\n- Wait, I should check `source_routing` for `chapter_ids`. P0056 is assigned to CH03. P0311 is assigned to CH03. I will keep them.\n\n**Final Check on Constraints:**\n- \"Do not silently drop a routed source\".\n- \"Return JSON only\".\n- \"Use Chinese\".\n- \"Supplement requests must have targeted queries in English\".\n\nLet's construct the JSON.",
